<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids drop.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids drop.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat and soft white wheat bids dropped on Friday in line with weaker MGE wheat futures.</p>
<p>December MGE spring wheat futures lost seven cents to end at $4.13-1/2 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;Movement has been steady,&quot; one Minneapolis dealer said. But he noted that a lot of spring wheat is expected to come on stream in the next two weeks as elevators make room for corn and soybeans. That would pressure cash values, he said.</p>
<p>Also, the lack of moisture in many areas in Montana has limited winter wheat seedings, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still waiting for some rain,&quot; a Montana dealer said.  </p>
